-- title:
--   Isotypic embedding into a direct sum of copies of an irreducible
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $G = \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$. Let $V$ and $W$ be complex vector spaces (abelian groups with a $\mathbb{C}$-module structure) carrying actions of $G$ by additive maps, the actions commuting with the complex scalars. Suppose $V$ satisfies [`LocalNewvector.IsIrreducibleGLRep q V`](def/LocalNewvector_ConductorDatum.html#L102), i.e. $V$ contains a nonzero vector and every $\mathbb{C}$-subspace of $V$ stable under all $g \in G$ equals $\bot$ or $\top$. Let $\kappa$ be a type and $f : \kappa \to (V \to_{\mathbb{C}} W)$ a family of $\mathbb{C}$-linear maps with $f_i(x \cdot v) = x \cdot f_i(v)$ for all $i \in \kappa$, $x \in G$, $v \in V$, and suppose that the images span: $\bigsqcup_{i} \operatorname{range}(f_i) = \top$ as a supremum of $\mathbb{C}$-submodules of $W$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $\iota$ and a $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $L : W \to (\iota \to_{0} V)$ into the finitely supported functions $\iota \to V$ such that $L$ is injective and $L(x \cdot w) = x \cdot L(w)$ for all $x \in G$ and $w \in W$, the action on $\iota \to_0 V$ being coordinatewise. No continuity or smoothness is imposed; $L$ is only asserted to be an equivariant injection, not an isomorphism.
--
--   This is the structure theory of an isotypic representation — a representation generated by equivariant images of a single irreducible embeds equivariantly into a direct sum of copies of it — specialised to abstract complex representations of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$. It is used in the treatment of automorphic forms, by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_isIrreducibleGLRep_injective_linearMap_finsupp_of_isCuspConstituent`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_isIrreducibleGLRep_injective_linearMap_finsupp_of_isCuspConstituent) and [`AutomorphicForm.exists_isIrreducibleGLRep_linearMap_span_translate_realization_of_coversModCentre`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_isIrreducibleGLRep_linearMap_span_translate_realization_of_coversModCentre).
